Headline results:
- Accuracy is misleading here. The always-"no stroke" baseline gets 95.1% accuracy and catches no strokes.
- Class weighting fixes the cut-off, not the ranking. It doesn't improve ROC-AUC (0.85 either way), but it moves recall from 2% to 80%.
- Final test result: ROC-AUC 0.835 (95% CI 0.77–0.89). The model catches 40 of 50 strokes, with precision of 0.14.
- The model underfits; it doesn't overfit. The train/validation gap is only about 0.005. More data or adding squared terms doesn't help; the limit is how informative the features are.
- Main predictors: age (odds ratio 4.5 per standard deviation), missing BMI, hypertension and glucose. Heart disease is dropped because age and hypertension already carry its information.

